1
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:12,480
Final count: forty-two.

2
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:13,880
Forty-two?

3
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:20,040
Oh, that's not bad for a
pointy-eared Elvish princeling.

4
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:24,400
I myself am sitting pretty on forty-three.

5
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:30,360
Forty-three.

6
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:32,440
He was already dead.

7
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:34,520
He was twitching.

8
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:39,880
He was twitching because he's got my
axe embedded in his nervous system!

9
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:47,280
A family of field mice that climb up
sometimes, and they tickle me awfully.

10
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:50,560
Always trying to get something with it.

11
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:05,360
Many of these trees were my friends.

12
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:10,880
Creatures I had known from nut and acorn.

13
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:13,280
I'm sorry, Treebeard.

14
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:15,680
They had voices of their own.

15
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:19,680
Saruman!

16
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,800
A wizard should know better!

17
00:01:37,720 --> 00:01:44,280
There is no curse in Elvish,
Entish, or the tongues of Men

18
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:47,160
for this treachery.

19
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:14,800
Come, my friends.

20
00:02:16,080 --> 00:02:19,600
The Ents are going to war.

21
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:25,360
It is likely that we go to our doom.

22
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:32,000
The last march of the Ents.
